<p>Air travel across the Middle East—and well beyond—was thrown into chaos after U.S. and Israeli strikes on Iran led multiple countries to close, or partially close, their airspace. The result was mass flight cancellations and long reroutes that rippled across global schedules. Major hub airports that link Europe, Africa, and Asia—including Dubai and Doha—were hit especially hard, leaving many passengers stuck in transit or unable to depart. Several outlets said Iran launched retaliatory attacks in the region. SCMP described Iranian missiles hitting Gulf capitals and reported at least one death. The knock-on effects reached as far as India and Hong Kong, where airlines cancelled or rerouted international services; disruptions were reported at Delhi’s airport, and more than two dozen Middle East-bound flights from Hong Kong were affected. The situation is still shifting, but the immediate reality is straightforward: airspace restrictions meant to keep flights safe are reshaping routes worldwide, stretching travel times, and forcing airlines and airports into a scramble to rebook passengers and restore normal operations.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/LE8jVEMDjJEg0Bpgc6nMDUfwszGh2bNwc0hV6K7JUAIJo8aW-0f05wMXsx1crWKZUJd4Uk41pwRdHXqVj3HY1WwBwmh2v0PGGnH6iOuMIF1sruqe73MBM2faX2ljB98BRwMCzCXe9f5ha8SlA74VqqeV7eLOZ5lmkc3gbHAOYuWPTIJORkHd8UG9bEVfOg' alt='The check-in desk for Emirates airline at London Gatwick Airport after the airline paused operations to and from Dubai.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Flight counts: Major Middle Eastern airlines cancelled more than 1,800 flights during the airspace shutdowns, according to reporting that cited flight-tracking and industry data.</li><li>Hong Kong impact: At least 27 flights from Hong Kong to Middle East destinations were cancelled or delayed on Sunday, with passengers crowding the airport for updates, SCMP reported.</li><li>Delhi disruption: Airspace closures across West Asia triggered major delays and cancellations at Indira Gandhi International Airport in Delhi, stranding some international passengers as routings shifted.</li><li>Carrier actions: Emirates and Qatar Airways cancelled or rerouted flights, while Turkish Airlines suspended several routes until Monday, Euronews reported.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>United Arab Emirates authorities: The UAE announced a “temporary and partial closure” of its airspace, and flight tracking later showed no flight activity over the United Arab Emirates. (<a href='https://michaelwest.com.au/thousands-of-travellers-stranded-by-flight-disruptions/'>Michael West Media</a>)</li><li>FlightRadar24: FlightRadar24 pointed to typical daily movement levels at affected airports (including Dubai, Doha and Abu Dhabi), highlighting just how many journeys usually pass through these hubs. (<a href='https://michaelwest.com.au/thousands-of-travellers-stranded-by-flight-disruptions/'>Michael West Media</a>)</li><li>Kerala state administration: Kerala set up help desks and stepped up monitoring as cancellations and reroutes disrupted travel to and from West Asia, reflecting the state’s large expatriate population in the Gulf. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/videos/west-asia-tensions-flights-cancelled-across-india-kerala-on-high-alert/article70689245.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>Airlines and airports: Carriers and airports told passengers to expect cancellations, delays, and reroutes as countries closed airspace as a precaution, according to multiple reports. (<a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/02/28/us-and-israeli-strikes-on-iran-disrupt-regional-and-international-flights'>Euronews</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/02/28/world/middleeast/middle-east-airport-closures-emirates-qatar.html'>Middle East Airspace Closes as U.S.-Israeli Strikes Hit Iran</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/middle-east/article/3344995/us-iran-conflict-flares-thousands-middle-east-flights-cancelled-airspace-closed'>As US-Iran conflict flares, thousands of Middle East flights cancelled, airspace closed</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/videos/west-asia-tensions-flights-cancelled-across-india-kerala-on-high-alert/article70689245.ece'>Watch: West Asia Tensions: Flights cancelled across India, Kerala on high alert</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://michaelwest.com.au/thousands-of-travellers-stranded-by-flight-disruptions/'>Thousands of travellers stranded by flight disruptions</a> - michaelwest.com.au</li><li><a href='https://www.firstpost.com/india/flights-disrupted-at-delhi-airport-as-west-asia-airspace-closures-hit-international-routes-13984896.html'>Flights disrupted at Delhi airport as West Asia airspace closures hit international routes</a> - firstpost.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/u-s-israel-attack-on-iran-leaves-hundreds-of-thousands-of-travelers-stranded-by-flight-disruptions'>U.S.–Israel attack on Iran leaves hundreds of thousands of travelers stranded by flight disruptions</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/02/28/us-and-israeli-strikes-on-iran-disrupt-regional-and-international-flights'>US and Israeli strikes on Iran: regional and international flights disrupted</a> - euronews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/india-news/iran-israel-war-khamenei-dead-fliers-stuck-at-indian-airports-due-to-middle-east-crisis-after-us-israel-attack-iran-11152999#publisher=newsstand'>&quot;No Clue What To Do&quot;: Fliers Stuck At Indian Airports Due To Middle East Crisis</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/attack-iran-disrupts-flights-middle-east-130621827'>Attack on Iran disrupts flights across the Middle East and beyond</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.independent.co.uk/bulletin/news/dubai-flights-cancelled-iran-attack-airspace-airport-b2929467.html'>Iran, Iraq, Israel, Kuwait, Qatar, and Syria close their respective air